  <note>
    <content textType="body">
      <p>Stop four is validation, and it is the first gate. Every rule - card number, expiry, amount, currency - implements one interface and is discovered by Spring. That is the Strategy pattern doing real work: adding a new rule is literally adding a class, with no registry to update. Two behaviors I want to highlight: we collect all errors instead of stopping at the first, so the merchant gets one complete 400; and the rules are pure functions, which makes them the easiest code in the project to unit test.</p>
    </content>
  </note>
